# Builds

When a coding task that touches the Mac app is done, run a Debug build before stopping.

```sh
xcodebuild -scheme Cracker -destination 'platform=macOS,arch=arm64' -quiet build
```

- Use this to catch compile errors; it is not a release.
- Do not tag or ship just because the Debug build succeeded.
- If the build fails, fix it before considering the task done.
